{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795223,"nonce":"TaM8PbJUSogY6AdSai2Z0NcRjHc=","title":"Add Twitch accounts, EventSub chat and channel controls as a provider","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P2\n\nScope\nImplement a Twitch provider with scoped OAuth/account connection, supported channel metadata/status, EventSub chat/events, message sending/moderation only with required grants, and clear team-versus-audience labeling. Handle token rotation/revocation, event resubscription, network loss and API/rate-limit errors. Keep persistent provider connections outside hibernating room objects. Treat chat input as untrusted display data and do not convert it into editor/run commands.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nProvider fixtures and a separately authorized account test exercise connect/revoke/reconnect, duplicate events, unavailable channel, permission changes and failures while Jam remains active. Unsupported capabilities are not advertised. Twitch credentials and stream keys stay out of shared files/logs. Public viewer identity never grants room editing or private media access.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}